# Compilation artifacts are content-addressed: an approved control pins one by SHA-256 and
# the resolver hashes the file's bytes to prove it is the artifact named. Any line-ending
# translation changes those bytes and breaks every binding — silently, and only on the
# machines whose git converts, which is every Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true.
#
# `-text` tells git never to convert these, in either direction.
data/compilations/** -text
